## Smoke Test Summary

New test file:

```text
tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
```

The smoke uses isolated child processes so each scenario starts with fresh module/runtime state.

### Deterministic / mock modes

```text
mock-init-reset-prompt
mock-control-init-prompt-reset-prompt
mock-init-reset-prompt-after-config-override
```

These modes use a deterministic fake `node-llama-cpp` module and verify parent/worker lifecycle state without needing the real native runtime.

The mock coverage checks that:

- `initModel() -> resetModel() -> prompt()` completes;
- `resetModel()` disposes the initialized model stack before the post-reset prompt path;
- the control path `initModel() -> prompt() -> resetModel() -> prompt()` still completes;
- config override initialization followed by reset and prompt still completes;
- no prompt begins before reset disposal completes.

### Real-runtime modes

Required real modes:

```text
real-init-reset-prompt
real-init-prompt-reset-prompt-control
```

Optional real mode:

```text
real-init-reset-prompt-after-config-override
```

The optional config override real mode runs only when:

```bash
REAL_CONFIG_OVERRIDE_SMOKE=1 SMOKE_MODE=real-orchestrator node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
```

