## Michael-Local Real Runtime Validation

Command run by Michael:

```bash
SMOKE_MODE=real-orchestrator node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
```

Required real mode result:

```text
real-init-reset-prompt: PASS
```

Observed milestones:

```text
[OK] real initModel resolved
[OK] real resetModel resolved without prior prompt
[OK] real post-init-reset prompt result: 1. 100
[OK] real shutdown resolved
```

Required control mode result:

```text
real-init-prompt-reset-prompt-control: PASS
```

Observed milestones:

```text
[OK] real control initModel resolved
[OK] real control before-reset prompt result: ...
[OK] real control resetModel resolved
[OK] real control after-reset prompt result: ...
[OK] real control shutdown resolved
```

Both real child modes exited with code `0`.

Known warnings observed during real runtime testing:

```text
ExperimentalWarning: Importing JSON modules is an experimental feature and might change at any time
[node-llama-cpp] load: control-looking token: 128247 '</s>' was not control-type; this is probably a bug in the model. its type will be overridden
```

These warnings were already known from prior real-runtime smoke testing and did not fail the branch smoke.

---

## Result / Conclusion

The original caveat is considered **cleared for the default/base path** by focused real-runtime coverage.

The suspicious sequence:

```text
initModel() -> resetModel() -> prompt()
```

passed on Michael's real model/runtime setup.

The control sequence:

```text
initModel() -> prompt() -> resetModel() -> prompt()
```

also passed.

No runtime code patch is recommended from the evidence gathered in this branch.

---

## Important Caveats

### 1. This branch clears the focused default path, not every possible reset/profile variant

The required real modes passed. The optional real config-override mode was included but was not part of the required reported run.

If future work changes effective config handling, retry profiles, or reset re-init behavior, the optional config-override mode may be useful as an additional regression check.

### 2. Prompt content is not semantically asserted

The real model prompt outputs are intentionally not judged for semantic quality. The test only verifies lifecycle completion, stream/done settlement, and post-reset prompt viability.

### 3. No hard-kill behavior was added

This branch does not alter the native operation timeout policy. It does not terminate active worker threads before native cooperative boundary settlement.

True hard-kill containment remains a separate future design direction, likely requiring a child-process native execution boundary.

